  m_text: Legend tells that when the emperor came to Alexandria and ordered sacrifices
    to the Roman gods, a young woman named Catherine stepped forward. She spoke openly
    of her Christian faith, and the emperor summoned fifty scholars to challenge
    her. They came to change her mind. By the end of the debate, she had changed
    theirs.
